### Check 2 — Regression smoke

**One verb runs the gates and owns the marker.** It takes the gates from the project's CI (a
narrower guess passes locally, fails on push) and marks only a pass on an unchanged tree.

{% if is_codex %}
```
Bash("uv run --with {{ harness_maker_src_path }} hm observability.verification_cache run --root . --mode relevant{% if light_check | default(false) %} --spec-slug <slug>{% endif %}")
```
{% else %}
```bash
!uv run --with {{ harness_maker_src_path }} hm observability.verification_cache run --root . --mode relevant --timeout-s 3600 --deadline-s 3600{% if light_check | default(false) %} --spec-slug <slug>{% endif %}
```
{% endif %}

{% if is_codex %}Foreground call: the defaults (540 s/gate, 570 s total) report their own timeout.{% else %}Run it in the **background** (`run_in_background: true`): a full suite outlives the 10-minute
foreground cap.{% endif %} Branch on the `"exit"` field of the JSON line it prints, never on the
host's status; no JSON line = not a pass.

- `0` → PASS (`cached: true` = its own marker reused). {% if light_check | default(false) %}Go on to gate 3.{% else %}Skip to Check 3.{% endif %}
- `1` → a gate failed or timed out, not a pass — stderr names the command and its output tail.
- `4` → the tree changed during the run, not a pass (stderr lists the paths); re-run.
- Killed by the host (no exit code) → not a pass, no marker.
{% if light_check | default(false) %}- `3` → degraded: neither readable CI nor a usable SPEC plan (stderr says why), not a pass here:
  the light check never guesses the gates, so it writes no record and review runs next.
{% else %}- `3` → degraded: no readable CI (stderr says why). Only then:

